.SH "NAME"
pcre2-config \- program to return PCRE2 configuration == SYNOPSIS
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
pcre2\-config  [\-\-prefix] [\-\-exec\-prefix] [\-\-version]
             [\-\-libs8] [\-\-libs16] [\-\-libs32] [\-\-libs\-posix]
             [\-\-cflags] [\-\-cflags\-posix]
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
\fBpcre2\-config\fP returns the configuration of the installed PCRE2 libraries
and the options required to compile a program to use them. Some of the options
apply only to the 8\-bit, 16\-bit, or 32\-bit libraries, respectively, and are not
available for libraries that have not been built. If an unavailable option is
encountered, the "usage" information is output.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\fB\-\-prefix\fP
.RS 4
Writes the directory prefix used in the PCRE2 installation for
architecture\-independent files (\fI/usr\fP on many systems, \fI/usr/local\fP on
some systems) to the standard output.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-exec\-prefix\fP
.RS 4
Writes the directory prefix used in the PCRE2 installation for
architecture\-dependent files (normally the same as \fB\-\-prefix\fP) to the
standard output.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP
.RS 4
Writes the version number of the installed PCRE2 libraries to the standard
output.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-libs8\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to link
with the 8\-bit PCRE2 library (\fB\-lpcre2\-8\fP on many systems).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-libs16\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to link
with the 16\-bit PCRE2 library (\fB\-lpcre2\-16\fP on many systems).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-libs32\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to link
with the 32\-bit PCRE2 library (\fB\-lpcre2\-32\fP on many systems).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-libs\-posix\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to link with
PCRE2\(cqs POSIX API wrapper library (\fB\-lpcre2\-posix\fP \fB\-lpcre2\-8\fP on many
systems).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-cflags\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to compile
files that use PCRE2 (this may include some \fB\-I\fP options, but is blank on
many systems).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-cflags\-posix\fP
.RS 4
Writes to the standard output the command line options required to compile
files that use PCRE2\(cqs POSIX API wrapper library (this may include some
\fB\-I\fP options, but is blank on many systems).
.RE
